%% Eraser lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no eraser session" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No eraser corridor, candidate cache, overlay preview,
    or eraser-owned commit intent exists. Generic pointer
    session owns down admission and one active routing token.
  end note

  Idle --> DownAdmission: generic pointer session admits finite normalized down
  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()
  Idle --> Idle: stale move/up/cancel or invalid down / no eraser session

  state "Down admitted by pointer session" as DownAdmission
  note right of DownAdmission
    Admission requires the active token, session id, controllerEpoch,
    draw mode, eraser tool, finite point, and finite thickness.
    Pointer id is only the routing token.
  end note

  DownAdmission --> Previewing: bind eraser session and publish first corridor point
  DownAdmission --> Idle: wrong mode/tool or non-finite facts / reject without preview
  DownAdmission --> Disposed: disposed runtime / StateError

  state "Active eraser preview" as Previewing {
    [*] --> CorridorPreview

    state "Overlay corridor preview" as CorridorPreview
    note right of CorridorPreview
      Corridor points are world-space preview facts only.
      Updates request overlay repaint only.
    end note

    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: same-token same-controllerEpoch finite move / append corridor
    CorridorPreview --> CandidateRefresh: same-token same-controllerEpoch finite move / refresh candidates
    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, or non-finite move / ignore
    CorridorPreview --> TerminalGate: same-token up
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: same-token cancel
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: mode change
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: interactive=false
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: loadDocument success after prepared replacement
    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: loadDocument failure / preserve if pointer session preserves
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: runtime.dispose()

    state "Read-only candidate refresh" as CandidateRefresh
    note right of CandidateRefresh
      Query SpatialKernel with corridor envelope inflated by
      eraserThickness / 2 + hitPadding + 4.0. Resolve committed
      candidates by generation and structuralRevision, then run
      exact segment-to-family geometry checks for deletable
      non-background content elements. Preview budget is 512
      candidates / 4096 exact checks per sample. No committed
      mutation occurs in preview.
    end note

    CandidateRefresh --> CorridorPreview: replace overlay preview and session candidate facts
    CandidateRefresh --> CorridorPreview: no candidates / preview remains corridor only
    CandidateRefresh --> CorridorPreview: budget exceeded / corridor-only preview, no partial tentative ids

    state "Terminal up gate" as TerminalGate
    note right of TerminalGate
      Terminal commit is allowed only for same token, same controllerEpoch,
      finite terminal point, and candidate/geometry facts derived
      from the final corridor. Terminal budget is 4096 candidates /
      32768 exact checks.
    end note

    TerminalGate --> CleanupOnly: stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, non-finite, or invalid terminal
    TerminalGate --> FinalCandidates: valid terminal / query final corridor

    state "Final candidate and geometry check" as FinalCandidates
    FinalCandidates --> EraseDecision: compute erased ids from valid deletable content candidates
    FinalCandidates --> CleanupOnly: budget exceeded / cleanup no-op, no partial erase

    state EraseDecision <<choice>>
    EraseDecision --> CleanupOnly: erased ids empty
    EraseDecision --> EditCommit: erased ids non-empty

    state "EditKernel erase commit" as EditCommit
    note right of EditCommit
      InteractionEngine opens a synchronous EditKernel session
      and removes erased ids through draft mutations only.
      The Store is never mutated directly.
    end note

    EditCommit --> CommitSucceeded: EditKernel outcome installed commit
    EditCommit --> CleanupOnly: EditKernel rejected, rolled back, or threw

    state "Commit succeeded" as CommitSucceeded
    note right of CommitSucceeded
      Atomic install is the commit boundary. Removed ids drive
      exact touched set, spatial removals, projection eviction,
      main repaint, and deferred erase action materialization.
    end note

    CommitSucceeded --> CleanupBeforeSignals: close edit handle and clear eraser session

    state "Cleanup before public state" as CleanupBeforeSignals
    note right of CleanupBeforeSignals
      Eraser action and state/repaint notifications are
      published only after successful commit and session cleanup.
    end note

    CleanupBeforeSignals --> PublishCommitSignals: overlay cleanup queued

    state "Publish erase action and runtime state" as PublishCommitSignals
    PublishCommitSignals --> [*]: publish main repaint, overlay cleanup, CanvasRuntimeState, erase action

    state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
    note left of CleanupOnly
      Cancel, mode change, load success, interactive=false,
      dispose, stale or invalid terminal, empty erased ids,
      eraser budget exceeded with no partial erase,
      and EditKernel failure clear preview/session only.
      Empty/no-op cleanup publishes no erase action or document
      state. Active preview cleanup publishes CanvasRuntimeState
      with updated preview revision.
    end note

    CleanupOnly --> CleanupOverlay: clear corridor, candidates, token binding, and session facts

    state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as CleanupOverlay
    CleanupOverlay --> [*]: request overlay repaint only
  }

  Previewing --> Idle: eraser session closed
  Previewing --> Disposed: dispose cleanup complete

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: pointer sample or mutating operation / StateError

  note left of Previewing
    Forbidden paths:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no main-scene preview during eraser preview;
    no direct DocumentStoreKernel mutation;
    no full committed mutation during preview;
    no partial erase on budget exceeded;
    no legacy source as normative architecture.
  end note
